        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "**SP09 \u2014 Change the window, preserve the units**  \n**Which normalization preserves amplitude, and which preserves power?**  \nRun 2 s at 128 Hz; analyze 0\u20131 s, N=128. Compare Rectangular, Periodic Hann and Periodic Hamming. The calibration peak stays 2 V.  \nCG: 1, 0.5, 0.54; ENBW: 1, 1.5, 1.362826 Hz. Use All inputs. Edit weak amplitude 0.05 \u2192 0.1; inspect the mixture near 24 Hz.  \n[Open SP09 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/SP09-window-normalization/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT teaching materials](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/2-161-signal-processing-continuous-and-discrete-fall-2008/resources/lecture_12/) \u00b7 [S7 spectrum guide](qrc:/s7studio/help/docs/STUDIO_SPECTRUM.md)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 1298,
          "height": 340,
          "font_size": 18
        }
      }
